      "title": "News live: Hanson says Australians should be able to use super for cost-of-living pressures",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/16/politics-reactions-nsw-gun-buyback-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-one-nation-bird-flu-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow live updates</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Prime Minister Anthony Albanese has just been speaking alongside the New South Wales Premier, Chris Minns:</p><p>He said:</p><p>Australians are quite rightly proud of our gun laws but the the fact is there are more guns in Australia today than there were at the the time of dealing with the Port Arthur gun buyback that occurred Arthur gun buyback that occurred under the Howard government.</p><p>These arrangements are available to every state and territory, and this reform comes on top of previous reforms that have been undertaken by my government in partnership with states and territories in particular the first ever development of a national firearms register.</p><p>In some ways, I feel that you should give them their money now, and let them help them with the cost of living.</p><p>It is their money; they’ve they’ve sacrificed it in lieu of pay. So, in a lot of cases, people want it.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/16/politics-reactions-nsw-gun-buyback-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-one-nation-bird-flu-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-16T00:21:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "One Nation senator says parents who support their trans children are engaging in ‘child abuse’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/16/one-nation-tyron-whitten-comments-parents-trans-children-abuse-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>‘There’s male, there’s female, and then there’s mental illness,’ Tyron Whitten says on YouTube show</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One Nation senator Tyron Whitten has claimed parents supporting their children who identify as transgender are engaging in “child abuse”, telling a fringe YouTube show: “there’s male, there’s female, and then there’s mental illness”.</p><p>Guardian Australia has unearthed several incendiary comments from Whitten and fellow One Nation senators Pauline Hanson and her longtime lieutenant Malcolm Roberts, about transgender Australians.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/16/one-nation-tyron-whitten-comments-parents-trans-children-abuse-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-15T20:00:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Naidoc awards honour ‘fearless, brilliant’ promoter of First Nations culture Rhoda Roberts",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/16/naidoc-awards-2026-rhoda-roberts-first-nations-honour-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Proud Widjabul Wiyebal woman of the Bundjalung nation recognised posthumously with the lifetime achievement award</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One of Australia’s greatest cultural ambassadors has been recognised posthumously for dedicating her life to sharing, preserving and promoting First Nations culture through language, dance and ceremony.</p><p>A proud Widjabul Wiyebal woman of the Bundjalung nation, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/mar/21/rhoda-roberts-indigenous-cultural-leader-who-introduced-the-term-welcome-to-country-dies-aged-66\">Rhoda Roberts died in March</a> aged 66. On Saturday night in Alice Springs, she was posthumously awarded the lifetime achievement award at the Naidoc awards.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/16/naidoc-awards-2026-rhoda-roberts-first-nations-honour-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-15T14:01:01"
